00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.680
have some ideas about areas

226
00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.680
that might have weird errors.

227
00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.640
Flaky tests were really interesting.

228
00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:21.080
I said that like AWS was AWS converges to truth over time,

229
00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:25.480
which is really annoying and this wasted a huge amount of time.

230
00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.640
I like

231
00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:32.160
never have flaky tests with AI is my hard rule.

232
00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.080
Just fix them immediately.

233
00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.880
It's weird things go wrong sometimes.

234
00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:42.880
It decides that the training data says that developers never fix flaky tests,

235
00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:43.880
so we ignore them.

236
00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:46.400
And I then shout at it and say no.

237
00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.760
In this code base, we fix our flaky tests.

238
00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:53.360
It says so in the agents.md file, and you're ignoring it again.

239
00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:57.520
But somehow the training data says no one fixes flaky test,

240
00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:58.880
which was definitely true.

241
00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.000
I've worked in many places that had a lot of flaky tests.

242
00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:05.240
Sometimes with the AWS tests, it decides

243
00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:09.360
that I do changes their behavior every day.

244
00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:14.720
We'll just change the code to match again because we must match AWS behavior.

245
00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.880
So we and then it's like, oh no, it's changed back again.

246
00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.400
Okay, well we'll change that again.

247
00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:22.520
